A||||13||Rodrv6||Just Getting Acquainted||||6
Z||000000||Rodrv6||11-16-1999||10:51 PM||||I am a newcomer to the Fiero Forum and have found it to be the best Fiero site I've found.  I bought a 1984 SE new in Feb. '84 to use as a daily driver. Over the years I have done all of my own maintennance up to and including combining my original red '84 with a black '84 (long story).  I still drive the car daily and have put 327,000 miles on the odometer.  Two years ago I dissassembled the entire car down to the bare space frame.  Aside from several worn out suspension pieces the only other problem was a rusted out battery box.  I had rebuilt the engine and manual transaxle a year or so earlier, so I didn't go into them.  I replaced the worn and rusted stuff, repainted the body panels, and reassembled the car. It's almost like driving a new one! Several friends questioned my sanity for sinking so much time and money into "an old car" but it was worth all of it. I have thoroughly enjoyed my Fiero over the years and plan to keep it indefinatly.  I would enjoy hearing from any of you who have stacked on the miles like me and what problems you may have come across.||||reg||6
Z||000001||turbo86se||11-16-1999||11:27 PM||||Wow, glad to hear of you dedication to <BR>your prized Fiero! I don't think I've <BR>ever heard of a Fiero with that many <BR>miles! My mechanic has a 88 Formula, it <BR>just turned 200,000 miles! You wouldn't <BR>know it if you looked at it or drove it, <BR>everything is mint! Lately he has put <BR>some work into it, such as a head gasket <BR>set, fuel pump, radiator, and brakes. The <BR>engine runs superb! You're right, this is <BR>a great Forum. Everyone gets along and <BR>has fun here, and that's what's <BR>important! I've been on the Fiero list, <BR>and really got tired of all the flame <BR>wars. Good to have you on the Forum!||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||11-16-1999||11:27 PM||||How about your long story.......Welcome to the Forum. I've not been on it for long either. It's always fun and informative to talk about Fieros with other Fierofiles. No long storys about my Fiero yet. Just got it in March||||reg||7
Z||000003||AL||11-16-1999||11:32 PM||||WELL I BOUGHT MY 86.5 GT ABOUT THREE MONTHS AGO,I TOOK THE HEADS OFF AND PUT THEM BACK IN AFTER THE MACHINE SHOP FINISHED WITH THEM, THEN I DID THE CAP ROTOR, WIRES, SPARK PLUGS, BELTS,TRANNY SERVICE.SENT THE RADIATOR OUT AND DID THE COOLANT,I ALSO REPLACED HEATER CORE AND ALL HOSES. SO FAR THE CAR IS A DELIGHT TO DRIVE, AND NO PROBLEMS YET.I PAID 900 CLAMS FOR IT AND SPENT ANOTHER 500, TO BRING THE TOTAL TO 1400.AND LIKE YOU I WILL BE REBUILDING THE WHOLE ENGINE WHEN IT WILL BE TIME, I GOT THE CAR WITH 74K ON THE ODOMETER AND I'M BARELY HITTING 2000 MILES MORE SINCE I FIXED IT. I ALSO CHANGED ALL VAC LINES. GOOD LUCK AND WELCOME TO THE ONLY FORUM DEDICATED TO THE BEST MID ENGINE CAR, LONG LIVE THE FIERO.    ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||11-17-1999||07:13 AM||||Hi,<P>Welcome to the forum.  I'd say welcome to the World of Fieros but apparently you are the old timer here with the most longevity in Fieros.  COngratulations on maintaining your car for so long.  I usually keep my cars for many years but I've never racked as many miles as you have.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||11-17-1999||08:48 AM||||Welcome, Rodrv6 (can I call you Rod?).  I really respect you putting all that time and effort into your 84.  Makes me feel guilty for selling my original 84!  <P>Is your 84 red or black now?  I saw a black Fiero coupe (uncertain of year) with black 14" alloys at the 1996 Nationals in Indy - he had over 300,000 mi on his.  Was it you, by any chance?  Or do we have at least two 300K cars out there?||||reg||1
Z||000006||RZURCTN||11-17-1999||11:13 AM||||Congrats on finding a well kept secret, The Fiero Forum!  I am sure that with the extensive knowledge you bring to the table you will become an invaluable asset to the rest of us.  A complete teardown!  Wow!  If I only had the time!  Watch out Theogre,  you may yet have a rival!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rodrv6||11-17-1999||11:30 AM||||Here is the "long story" about my Fiero(s).  In the summer of 1992 a coworker asked me if I might be interested in purchasing his black '84 SE.  It had a blown motor and some chassis rust (New Jersey car), but was otherwise in excellent condition. His car also had a moonroof and tilt column that I did not.  My red SE had about 180,000 miles by then and was showing some signs of wear.  The left front corner had been rearranged in a traffic accident, the drivers seat was getting somewhat tattered, and the transaxle was beginning to make expensive noises.  The price was right so I bought the black one and towed it home.  About two weeks later the transaxle died completely, so I parked both cars in the garage and began taking pieces off of them.  I picked out the best ones and hung them on the good chassis.  When I was done I had a black SE with most of the options available that year.  My engine was a lot newer than the rest of the car since Pontiac was kind enough to GIVE me a new long block as part of the fire recall. The car had 99,600 miles on it when they swapped engines for me.  That is the best deal I have ever gotten from a dealer!!<BR>I have never had the car in Indiana, so there must be at least one other 300k Fiero out there somewhere!<BR>Rod||||reg||6
Z||000008||Ditz88GT||11-17-1999||01:19 PM||||Welcome Rod!  This is a great forum with lots of very good info.  Just wondering what is the most miles anyone has seen on a Fiero.  The most I ever saw was 130,000 on my first Fiero.  That really pales in comparison to over 300 but I'm curious what is the most out there.  Anyway welcome Rod and we're glad to have you.||||reg||14
Z||000009||lennyb4||11-17-1999||01:30 PM||||My neighbor has a jet black GT, i mean this car is showroom condition inside and out. He has 245,000 miles on it and loves it to death.I just hope that i can get that many out of mine.||||reg||10
Z||000010||batboy||11-17-1999||02:42 PM||||My 85 GT that I bought from the original owner this summer now has close to 150,000 miles on it.<P>I personally put over 50,000 miles in three years on my 87 SE, it presently has 130,000 on the odometer, but the engine is toast now.<P>I'm the second owner of my rusty but trusty Suburban with 260,000 miles on it (well over half of which I put on it) with no major work done to the engine yet (other than new water pump, alternator, etc.). The secret? Regular oil changes.||||reg||1
Z||000011||DJRice||11-18-1999||08:49 AM||||My 1987 SE with the lean mean six machine just turned 140k miles last weekend and she still will 'ride out'...||||reg||1
Z||000012||RFMike||11-18-1999||07:23 PM||||Welcome aboard, Rod. Yes, this is a great site.  <BR>My 86 GT now has 149,000 on it.  I bought it with 120,000 on it, completely stock. I've replaced the alternator and tires, some little stuff.  Needs some suspension work, coming up next. It still runs great, very strong. If the engine ever wears out, I'll rebuild it.  I plan on keeping this car forever.  At 33,000 miles a year, if I don't move closer to work, I could set the alltime record.  I can dream, can't I?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Scott2M4||11-19-1999||06:49 AM||||117,000 on my 1987 4 cylinder coupe.  The engine is still smooth, quiet and smoke-free.<P>I constantly get comments from people saying they can't believe the car is 13 years old because it looks so good!  Thank you, Pontiac, for going with the plastic body (many same year MR2s, CRXs and RX-7s are losing their bodies to rust)!<p>[This message has been edited by Scott2M4 (edited 11-19-1999).]||||reg||1
